  "transcription_notes": [
    "The article names Table 10's method the Wilcoxon rank sum test; this artifact does not relabel it as the paired Wilcoxon signed-rank test used by Mayfly's comparison framework.",
    "The +/−/= summary is preserved in the source's printed symbol order. Combining the zero '+' totals with the prose that AOBLMOA has no significant disadvantage implies that '-' denotes an AOBLMOA advantage, but the absent raw samples prevent an independent direction check.",
    "Table 11 assigns tied algorithms the same integer rank without averaging the occupied ranks. The published rank rows and their resulting mean ranks are preserved exactly.",
    "The source reports p-values rounded to the displayed precision; 1.73e-6 and 3.79e-6 are transcribed values, not recomputed statistics."
  ],
  "reproduction_blockers": [
    "Neither the article nor linked repository provides the 30 raw result samples for every algorithm and benchmark case, so the published tests cannot be recomputed.",
    "The linked repository has no 30-run table driver, statistical-analysis driver, or published seed schedule and supplies only the f1 benchmark evaluator.",
    "Mayfly's comparison framework implements paired Wilcoxon signed-rank tests, while the paper explicitly reports independent-run Wilcoxon rank-sum tests.",
    "The paper/code/library AOBLMOA fidelity conflicts recorded in aoblmoa-2023-tables5-6.json remain open."
  ],
